{
  "title": "CanvasSizingContext",
  "description": "What a CanvasSizing is given to work with, and the one channel through which it changes the canvas. A context describes the application as it stood when the policy was attached. The application hands out a fresh one on every attach, so a change it cannot express - a new base resolution, a canvas moved to another parent - reaches a policy by re-attaching it rather than by mutating what it already holds.",
